 "estimated_cost_usd": 0.8098,
 "summary": "Security analysis of `psutil-7.1.2` identified potential Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) risks (CWE-1333) in internal parsing logic, particularly within `_pslinux.py` and `_psaix.py`. These regexes parse system output (e.g., `/proc` filesystem, command outputs), which generally minimizes the attack surface unless an attacker can influence system configuration or process names to trigger pathological cases. The analysis also confirmed the extensive use of command execution (CWE-78) as part of the library's core functionality (e.g., on AIX/SunOS), which appears properly encapsulated but remains a sensitive area. No high-severity injection or deserialization vulnerabilities were found.",
